> m1(x: i8) = match x { 0 => 1, 1 | 2 => 5, 3..9 => 7, _ => 9 }
> domain m1
domain of m1:
  x: i8, -128..127
  no conditions: total on its parameter types
  defined at 256 of 256 points
  over all 256 points of the domain
> range m1
range of m1 -> int:
  1..9
  fits in u4
  over all 256 points of the domain
> wrap m1
wrap analysis of m1:
  no wrapping or rounding operations
  end to end: equals the mathematical (unbounded) result everywhere
  over all 256 points of the domain
> p1(x: u8) = { x if x < 3, 100 otherwise }
> domain p1
domain of p1:
  x: u8, 0..255
  no conditions: total on its parameter types
  defined at 256 of 256 points
  over all 256 points of the domain
> range p1
range of p1 -> u8:
  0..100   (4 distinct values)
  values: 0..2, 100
  fits in u7
  over all 256 points of the domain
> wrap p1
wrap analysis of p1:
  no wrapping or rounding operations
  end to end: equals the mathematical (unbounded) result everywhere
  over all 256 points of the domain
> w1(x: i8, y: i8) = x + y where y > x
> domain w1
domain of w1:
  x: i8, -128..127
  y: i8, -128..127
  where y > x
  C assumes x + y does not overflow i8  (signed overflow)
  defined at 32640 of 32640 points
  C undefined behaviour at 8128 points, e.g. x=-128, y=-127
  over all 32640 points of the domain
> range w1
range of w1 -> i8:
  -128..127   (256 distinct values)
  fits in i8
  over all 32640 points of the domain
> wrap w1
wrap analysis of w1:
  x + y   (i8)
      nuw fails: unsigned wrap at 16256 points, e.g. x=-128, y=-127
      nsw fails: signed wrap at 8128 points, e.g. x=-128, y=-127  <- UB in C; a compiler assumes it cannot happen
  end to end: differs from the mathematical result at 8128 points, e.g. x=-128, y=-127
  over all 32640 points of the domain
> w2(x: u16 in 0..31, n: u16 in 0..5) = x << n where x < 1 << n
> domain w2
domain of w2:
  x: u16, 0..31
  n: u16, 0..5
  where x < 1 << n
  requires 0 <= n < 16  (shift amount; C UB otherwise)
  defined at 63 of 63 points
  over all 63 points of the domain
> range w2
range of w2 -> u16:
  0..992   (47 distinct values)
  values: 0, 2, 4, 8, 12, 16, 24, 32, 40, 48, 56, 64, 80, 96, 112, 128, 144, 160, 176, 192, 208, 224, 240, 256, ...
  fits in u10
  over all 63 points of the domain
> c1(x: i8) = x > 0 ? x - 1 : 0
> wrap c1
wrap analysis of c1:
  x - 1   (i8)
      nuw holds
      nsw holds (C requires it: signed overflow is UB)
  end to end: equals the mathematical (unbounded) result everywhere
  over all 256 points of the domain
> domain c1
domain of c1:
  x: i8, -128..127
  C assumes x - 1 does not overflow i8  (signed overflow)
  defined at 256 of 256 points
  over all 256 points of the domain
